##
#
# Supersonic channel flow past a cylinder in 3D at Mach 3, Section 5 and
# Figure 6 of [1].
#
# The geometry is a cylinder of diameter 0.5 centered along (0.6, 0, z) in
# a channel [0,4] x [-1,1] x [-1,1]; the 2D coarse mesh is extruded into 3D
# with 4 layers of hexahedra. The channel is initially filled with a
# uniform flow at Mach 3 (rho = 1.4, v = 3, p = 1, gamma = 1.4). On the
# left inflow boundary Dirichlet boundary conditions and on the right
# outflow boundary "do nothing" conditions are enforced. On all other
# boundaries (top, bottom, front, and back boundaries of the channel and
# the cylinder boundary) slip boundary conditions are enforced.
#
# Warning, this is a very large computation!
#
# The chosen refinement level 8 corresponds to around 1.8B gridpoints as in
# Figure 6 of [1], which shows a snapshot at t = 5.0. Figure 6 was computed
# with an earlier version of the solver using a second-order SSP
# Runge-Kutta scheme (ssprk 22) on 30720 MPI ranks with an average
# time-step size of 6.0e-05 (about 83k time steps). Refinement levels 6 and
# 7 correspond to 29M and 228M gridpoints, respectively. The coarse mesh
# (208 gridpoints) is the one of [1]; this is a reconstruction of the
# original configuration.
#
# Output reduced vtks only containing hexahedra that intersect with the
# cutplanes x, y, z, and x^2+y^2-0.25*0.25 (as configured down below in the
# "subsection I - VTUOutput"). Figure 6 of [1] shows a Schlieren plot and
# the magnitude of the vorticity on cutplanes.
#
# [1] M. Maier, M. Kronbichler. Efficient parallel 3D computation of the
#     compressible Euler equations with an invariant-domain preserving
#     second-order finite-element scheme. ACM Trans. Parallel Comput.,
#     8(3):16:1-30, 2021. DOI 10.1145/3470637, arXiv:2007.00094
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = mach3-cylinder-3d

  set tasks             = vtu levelsets

  set final time        = 5.00
  set timer granularity = 0.10
end


subsection B - Equation
  set dimension = 3
  set equation  = euler
  set gamma     = 1.4
end


subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry            = cylinder

  set mesh refinement     = 8

  subsection cylinder
    set height          = 2
    set length          = 4
    set object diameter = 0.5
    set object position = 0.6
  end
end


subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = uniform

  set direction     = 1, 0, 0
  set position      = 1, 0, 0

  set perturbation  = 0

  subsection uniform
    set primitive state = 1.4, 3, 1
  end
end


subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min               = 0.90
  set cfl max               = 0.90
  set cfl recovery strategy = none

  set time stepping scheme  = ssprk 22
end


subsection I - VTUOutput
  subsection levelsets
    set manifolds             = x, y, z, x^2+y^2-0.25*0.25
    set vtu output quantities = rho, m_1, m_2, m_3, E, schlieren_rho, vorticity_v_1

    set use mpi io            = true
    set schlieren beta        = 10
  end
end
